    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "In the presence of noise the blowup time becomes a random quantity, and it is interesting to determine its statistics. One way of addressing this class of problems is to interpret Eq. (1) as the equation of motion of an overdamped particle, with the coordinate n = n(t), in a repulsive potential V (n) ∼ −n3. By adding a noise term to Eq. (1), one turns this mean-field equation into a Langevin equation:"
